<title>FRANCE: French official economic forecasts - breakdown.</title>
<headline>French official economic forecasts - breakdown.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government gave the following economic forecasts. The figures in brackets are the previous figures for 1996 and 1997 published in the French budget on September 18, 1996: (figures are percentage changes unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>					1996	    1997	     1998</p>
<p> GDP (bln Ffr)		   7,884 (7,893)  8,147 (8,170)  8,476</p>
<p> GDP				  1.3   (1.3)   2.3   (2.3)    2.8</p>
<p> Public deficit/GDP	     4.1   (4.0)   3.0   (3.0)    2.8</p>
<p> Household Consumption	  2.3   (2.1)   1.4   (1.4)    1.9</p>
<p> Business  Investment	  -0.8   (2.0)   3.0   (5.0)    5.4</p>
<p> Internal demand (ex-stocks)  1.6   (1.9)   1.7   (1.8)    2.2</p>
<p> Stock change contribution   -0.7  (-0.6)   0.3   (0.5)    0.2</p>
<p> Exports			    3.4   (2.2)   5.3   (5.1)    5.7</p>
<p> Imports			    1.8   (2.4)   4.3   (5.3)    4.5</p>
<p>Consumer prices</p>
<p>   annual average		 1.8   (2.1)   1.5   (1.5)    1.5</p>
<p>   year-end period		1.6   (1.5)   1.5   (1.5)    1.5</p>
<p> Savings Ratio (pct)	   12.3  (12.6)  12.5  (12.6)   12.8</p>
<p> Trade balance (bln Ffr)	122  (100) 130-140  (100)  160-170</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
